@page
@model LynqMentrics.Pages.Privacy.CookiesModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cookie Policy";
}

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-300">
    <header class="border-b border-slate-800 pb-6">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white">Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400">Last Updated: 2026-08-03</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>This Cookie Policy explains how LynqMentrics, a service provided by KKGLabs, uses cookies and similar technologies when you visit or use our Service. It explains what these technologies are, why we use them, and your rights to control their use.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">2. What Are Cookies?</h2>
        <p>Cookies are small text files that are placed on your device (computer, tablet, or mobile phone) when you visit a website. They are widely used to make websites work efficiently and to provide information to the owners of the site. Similar technologies include local storage, web beacons, and pixels.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">3. Types of Cookies We Use</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-100">Strictly Necessary Cookies</h3>
        <p>These cookies are essential for the Service to function properly. They enable core features such as security, network management, and account authentication. These cookies cannot be disabled. Examples include:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Authentication/session cookies that keep you signed in.</li>
            <li>Security cookies that protect against fraudulent activity.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-100">Analytics Cookies</h3>
        <p>These cookies help us understand how visitors interact with the Service by collecting and reporting information anonymously. We use this data to improve our Service. They are only set after you give your consent via the cookie consent banner.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-100">Preference Cookies</h3>
        <p>These cookies enable the Service to remember information that changes how the Service behaves or looks, such as your preferred language or region.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 font-semibold text-slate-100">Marketing Cookies</h3>
        <p>We currently do not use marketing cookies. If we do in the future, we will update this policy and obtain your consent where required.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">4. Consent and Your Choices</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Strictly necessary cookies</span> are always set and do not require consent.</li>
            <li><span class="font-semibold text-slate-100">Non-essential cookies and third-party resources</span> (such as Google Fonts) are only loaded after you provide your consent via our cookie consent banner.</li>
            <li>You can change your preferences at any time by clicking the "Cookie Settings" link in the footer of our website.</li>
            <li>You can also control cookies through your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may prevent the Service from functioning correctly.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">5. How to Manage Cookies in Your Browser</h2>
        <p>You can set your browser to refuse all or some browser cookies, or to alert you when cookies are being sent. Refer to your browser's help documentation:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" class="text-brandCyan underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" class="text-brandCyan underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firefox</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" class="text-brandCyan underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Safari</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/manage-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-168dab11-0753-043d-7c16-ede5947fc64d" class="text-brandCyan underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Edge</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">6. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for other operational, legal, or regulatory reasons. We will notify you of any significant changes by posting the new Cookie Policy on our website and updating the "Last Updated" date.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">7. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions or concerns about this Cookie Policy, please contact us at <a href="mailto:jsmith.teamiis@gmail.com" class="text-brandCyan underline">jsmith.teamiis@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
</article>
